---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getLangFromUrl, useTranslations } from '../../../../i18n/utils';

const lang = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url);
const t = useTranslations(lang);
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`SuperFont Support - ${t('site.title')}`}
  description="How to install fonts with SuperFont, why installation finishes in Safari and Settings, common sticking points, and how to reach us."
  lang={lang}
>
  <div class="max-w-5xl w-full mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-36">
    <div class="text-center mb-16 md:mb-20">
      <span class="block text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-primary mb-3">SuperFont</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-text tracking-tight mb-4">Support</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-sub">Stuck on an install? Check the steps below first, then tell us if it still fails.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none
      prose-headings:font-semibold prose-headings:tracking-tight
      prose-h2:text-xl prose-h2:mt-12 prose-h2:mb-4
      prose-h3:text-base prose-h3:mt-8 prose-h3:mb-2
      prose-p:text-text-sub prose-p:leading-7
      prose-li:text-text-sub
      prose-strong:text-text prose-strong:font-medium
      prose-a:text-primary prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline
      prose-code:before:content-none prose-code:after:content-none
    ">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, bug reports, and feature requests all go to the address below.
        We reply within 7 business days.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email</strong>: <a href="mailto:contact@hyewoninsong.com">contact@hyewoninsong.com</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why installation finishes in Safari and Settings</h2>
      <p>
        iOS does not let apps install system fonts directly. Fonts can only be installed through a
        <strong>configuration profile</strong>, iOS's official route, and a profile is downloaded by Safari and installed by the Settings app.
        SuperFont builds the profile from the fonts you chose and hands it to Safari; the final "Install" button lives in Settings.
        Leaving the app is how iOS is designed, not an error.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everything happens on your device. The profile reaches Safari over an on-device connection only, and your font files are never uploaded anywhere.
      </p>

      <h2>Installation steps</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>In SuperFont, tap <strong>Install New Font</strong>, pick your font files, then tap <strong>Get Profile in Safari</strong>. Safari opens.</li>
        <li>When Safari asks "This website is trying to download a configuration profile", tap <strong>Allow</strong>. A "Profile Downloaded" notice appears.</li>
        <li>Open the <strong>Settings</strong> app. If a "Profile Downloaded" row is shown at the top, tap it.
          Otherwise go to <strong>General &gt; VPN &amp; Device Management</strong>.</li>
        <li>Tap the profile, tap <strong>Install</strong> in the top right, enter your device passcode, and tap <strong>Install</strong> once more.</li>
        <li>Return to SuperFont. It confirms which fonts are now installed.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Installed fonts are also listed under <strong>Settings &gt; General &gt; Fonts</strong>.</p>

      <h2>Common sticking points</h2>

      <h3>Safari never shows "Profile Downloaded"</h3>
      <p>
        Either "Ignore" was tapped in the download prompt, or another browser is set as the default.
        Go back to SuperFont, tap <strong>Get Profile in Safari</strong> again, and choose <strong>Allow</strong> this time.
        Profile downloads only work in Safari.
      </p>

      <h3>The profile is not in Settings</h3>
      <p>
        Check the "Downloaded Profile" row under <strong>Settings &gt; General &gt; VPN &amp; Device Management</strong>.
        If it is not there, the download did not complete in Safari. Repeat the steps above.
      </p>

      <h3>The font is installed but an app does not show it</h3>
      <p>
        The app you are using has to support user-installed fonts. Pages, Keynote, Numbers, Word, and Procreate do;
        apps such as Notes and Messages use system fonts only and will not show it.
        Fully quit and reopen the app you want to use the font in.
      </p>

      <h3>Removing fonts</h3>
      <p>
        Go to <strong>Settings &gt; General &gt; VPN &amp; Device Management</strong>, tap the profile SuperFont created, and choose <strong>Remove Profile</strong>.
        Every font in that profile is removed. Deleting the same entry from SuperFont's profile list tidies up the record inside the app.
      </p>

      <h3>It says the font is already installed</h3>
      <p>
        SuperFont unchecks faces that are already registered on the device in the preview. If you want to install them again anyway, check them and continue.
      </p>

      <h2>What to include in a report</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Device model and iOS version (Settings &gt; General &gt; About)</li>
        <li>Where it stopped: inside the app, in Safari, or in Settings</li>
        <li>The kind and number of font files (for example, 3 OTF files and 1 ZIP). You do not need to send the files themselves.</li>
        <li>A screen recording or screenshot, if you can</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        What SuperFont collects and where your font files stay is set out in the
        <a href="/en/apps/superfont/privacy/">SuperFont privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 text-center">
      <a href="/en/apps/superfont/" class="text-sm font-medium text-primary hover:underline">← SuperFont</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
